"It was a ride on a tractor\nOn the farm of potatoes\nIt was bumpy and will always be\nAnd that's the beauty, here it goes!\n\nThe potato I have\nHas two thoughts in two knees\nClashing always with each other\nLike in a fight of two bees\n\nSupports my tummy\nUnderstands my hunger\nThat's my potato\nWho was once a stranger\n\nTolerates the weather\nWhich sometimes I produce\nYet barely reacts on it\nAnd shows only the flower it use\n\nYes it sometimes stink\nAnd yes I clean that odor\nMany might find this disgusting\nBut that's my work which I'll always bear\n\nI feel alone the potato's here\nAnd vice versa like all times\nNot a burden but our duty\nLike the Pole Star which always shines\n\nYes we fight and will always do\nNeither's right and that's how it is\nI'll eat the potato if it stinks\nIt'll gobble me if I always step on it\n\nThe conclusion's simple\nThe potato's always here\nSo am I, never leaving the farm\nAnd we'll always be there to cheer"